\pard \fs24
{\plain \fs36 \i\f3\fs36 Concerning the Vigil}{\plain \fs24 \f3 \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3  \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 \par
}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 The Great Vigil, when observed, is the first service of Easter Day. It is \softline
celebrated at a convenient time between sunset on Holy Saturday and\par
}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 sunrise on Easter Morning.\par
}\pard \fs20\sl120\slmult1 
{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20  \par
}\pard \fs20
{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 The service normally consists of four parts:\par
}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 1.  The Service of Light.\par
}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 2.  The Service of Lessons.\par
}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 3.  Christian Initiation, or the Renewal of Baptismal Vows.\par
}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 4.  The Holy Eucharist with the administration of Easter Communion.\par
}\pard \fs20\sl120\slmult1 
{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 \par
}\pard \fs20
{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 It is customary for all the ordained ministers present, together with lay\par
}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 readers, singers, and other persons, to take active parts in the service.\par
}\pard \fs20\sl120\slmult1 
{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20  \par
}\pard \fs20
{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 The bishop, when present, is the chief celebrant, presides at Baptism\par
}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 and administers Communion, and normally preaches the sermon.\par
}\pard \fs20\sl120\slmult1 
{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 \par
}\pard \fs20
{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 The priests who are present share among them the reading of the Collects \softline
which follow each Lesson, and assist at Baptism and the Eucharist. In the \softline
absence of a bishop, a priest presides at the service.\par
}\pard \fs20\sl120\slmult1 
{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20  \par
}\pard \fs20
{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 It is the prerogative of a deacon to carry the Paschal Candle to its place, \par
}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 and to chant the Exsultet. Deacons likewise assist at Baptism and the Eucharist \softline
according to their order.\par
}\pard \fs20\sl120\slmult1 
{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20  \par
}\pard \fs20
{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 Lay persons read the Lessons and the Epistle, and assist in other ways.  A \par
}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 lay person may be assigned to chant the Exsultet. It is desirable that each \softline
Lesson be read by a different reader.\par
}\pard \fs20\sl120\slmult1 
{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20  \par
}\pard \fs20
{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 In the absence of a bishop or priest, a deacon or lay reader may lead the \par
}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 first two parts of the service, the Renewal of Baptismal Vows, and the Ministry \softline
of the Word of the Vigil Eucharist, concluding with the Prayers \par
}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 of the People, the Lord's Prayer, and the Dismissal.\par
}\pard \fs20\sl120\slmult1 
{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20  \par
}\pard \fs20
{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 A deacon may also, when the services of a priest cannot be obtained, and with \softline
the authorization of the bishop, officiate at public Baptism; and may administer \softline
Easter Communion from the Sacrament previously consecrated.\par
}\pard \fs20\sl120\slmult1 
{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20  \par
}\pard \fs20
{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 When the Vigil is not celebrated, the Service of Light may take place\par
}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 at a convenient time before the Liturgy on Easter Day.\par
}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20  }{\plain \fs24 \f3 \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 \par
}\column 
\pard \fs24
{\plain \fs48 \f3\fs48 The Great Vigil of Easter}{\plain \fs24 \f3 \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3  \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3  \par
}{\plain \fs36 \f3\fs36 The Lighting of the Paschal Candle}{\plain \fs24 \f3 \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3  \par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f3\fs20 In the darkness, fire is kindled; after which the Celebrant may address\par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f3\fs20 the people in these or similar words}{\plain \fs24 \f3 \par
}\pard \fs24\sl120\slmult1 
{\plain \fs24 \f3  \par
}\pard \fs24
{\plain \fs24 \f3 Dear friends in Christ: On this most holy night, in which our\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 Lord Jesus passed over from death to life, the Church invites\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 her members, dispersed throughout the world, to gather in\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 vigil and prayer.  For this is the Passover of the Lord, in which,\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 by hearing his Word and celebrating his Sacraments, we share\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 in his victory over death.\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3   \par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f3\fs20 The Celebrant may say the following prayer}{\plain \fs24 \f3 \par
}\pard \fs24\sl120\slmult1 
{\plain \fs24 \f3  \par
}\pard \fs24
{\plain \fs24 \f3 Let us pray.\par
}\pard \fs24\sl120\slmult1 
{\plain \fs24 \f3  \par
}\pard \fs24
{\plain \fs24 \f3 O God, through your Son you have bestowed upon your\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 people the brightness of your light: Sanctify this new fire, and\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 grant that in this Paschal feast we may so burn with heavenly\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 desires, that with pure minds we may attain to the festival of\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 everlasting light; through Jesus Christ our Lord.  }{\plain \fs24 \i\f3 Amen.}{\plain \fs24 \f3 \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3   \par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f3\fs20 The Paschal Candle is then lighted from the newly kindled fire, and the\par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f3\fs20 Deacon (the Celebrant if there is no deacon) bearing the Candle, leads the procession to the \softline
chancel, pausing three times and singing or saying}{\plain \fs24 \f3 \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3  \par
}\pard \fs24\tx-1440\tx-720\tx0\tx324\tx1044\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6154
{\plain \fs24 \f3 \tab \tab The light of Christ. \par
}\pard \fs24\fi-1044\li1044\tx-1440\tx-720\tx0\tx324\tx1044\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6154 
{\plain \fs20 \i\f3\fs20 People}{\plain \fs24 \f3  \ul0 \tab Thanks be to God.\par
}\pard \fs24\tx-1440\tx-720\tx0\tx324\tx1044\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6154
{\plain \fs24 \f3 \par
}\column 
\pard \fs20\tx-1440\tx-720\tx0\tx324\tx1044\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6154
{\plain \fs20 \i\f3\fs20 If candles have been distributed to members of the congregation, they are lighted from the \softline
Paschal Candle at this time.  Other candles and lamps in the church, except for those at the \softline
Altar, may also be lighted.\par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f3\fs20  \par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f3\fs20 The Paschal Candle placed in its stand.\par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f3\fs20  \par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f3\fs20 Then the Deacon, or other person appointed, standing near the Candle,\par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f3\fs20 sings or says the Exsultet, as follows (the indicated sections may be\par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f3\fs20 omitted)\par
}\pard \fs24\sl120\slmult1\tx-1440\tx-720\tx0\tx324\tx1044\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6154 
{\plain \fs20 \i\f3\fs20  }{\plain \fs24 \f3 \par
}\pard \fs24\tx-1440\tx-720\tx0\tx324\tx1044\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6154
{\plain \fs24 \f3 Rejoice now, heavenly hosts and choirs of angels, \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 and let your trumpets shout Salvation \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 for the victory of our mighty King. \par
}\pard \fs24\sl120\slmult1\tx-1440\tx-720\tx0\tx324\tx1044\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6154 
{\plain \fs24 \f3  \par
}\pard \fs24\tx-1440\tx-720\tx0\tx324\tx1044\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6154
{\plain \fs24 \f3 Rejoice and sing now, all the round earth, \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 bright with a glorious splendor, \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 for darkness has been vanquished by our eternal King. \par
}\pard \fs24\sl120\slmult1\tx-1440\tx-720\tx0\tx324\tx1044\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6154 
{\plain \fs24 \f3  \par
}\pard \fs24\tx-1440\tx-720\tx0\tx324\tx1044\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6154
{\plain \fs24 \f3 Rejoice and be glad now, Mother Church, \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 and let your holy courts, in radiant light, \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 resound with the praises of your people. \par
}\pard \fs24\sl120\slmult1\tx-1440\tx-720\tx0\tx324\tx1044\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6154 
{\plain \fs24 \f3  \par
}\pard \fs24\tx-1440\tx-720\tx0\tx324\tx1044\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6154
{\plain \fs24 \f3 All you who stand near this marvelous and holy flame, \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 pray with me to God the Almighty \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 for the grace to sing the worthy praise of this great light; \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 through Jesus Christ our Lord, \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 who lives and reigns with him, \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 in the unity of the Holy Spirit, \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 one God, for ever and ever.  }{\plain \fs24 \i\f3 Amen.}{\plain \fs24 \f3  \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3  \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 \tab \tab The Lord be with you. \par
}\pard \fs24\fi-1044\li1044\tx-1440\tx-720\tx0\tx324\tx1044\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6154 
{\plain \fs20 \i\f3\fs20 Answe}{\plain \fs24 \f3 r  \ul0 \tab And also with you. \par
}\pard \fs24\fi-1044\li1044\tx-1440\tx-720\tx0\tx324\tx1044\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6154 
{\plain \fs20 \i\f3\fs20 Deacon}{\plain \fs24 \f3   \ul0 \tab Let us give thanks to the Lord our God. \par
}\pard \fs24\fi-1044\li1044\tx-1440\tx-720\tx0\tx324\tx1044\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6154 
{\plain \fs20 \i\f3\fs20 Answer}{\plain \fs24 \f3   \ul0 \tab It is right to give him thanks and praise.\par
}\pard \fs24\tx-1440\tx-720\tx0\tx324\tx1044\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6154
{\plain \fs24 \f3  \par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f3\fs20 Deacon}{\plain \fs24 \f3 \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3  \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 It is truly right and good, always and everywhere, with our \par
}\column 
\pard \fs24\tx-1440\tx-720\tx0\tx324\tx1044\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6154
{\plain \fs24 \f3 whole heart and mind and voice, to praise you, the invisible,\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 almighty, and eternal God, and your only-begotten Son,\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 Jesus Christ our Lord; for he is the true Paschal Lamb, who\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 at the feast of the Passover paid for us the debt of Adam's sin,\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 and by his blood delivered your faithful people.\par
}\pard \fs24\sl120\slmult1\tx-1440\tx-720\tx0\tx324\tx1044\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6154 
{\plain \fs24 \f3  \par
}\pard \fs24\tx-1440\tx-720\tx0\tx324\tx1044\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6154
{\plain \fs24 \f3 This is the night, when you brought our fathers, the children\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 of Israel, out of bondage in Egypt, and led them through the\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 Red Sea on dry land.\par
}\pard \fs24\sl120\slmult1\tx-1440\tx-720\tx0\tx324\tx1044\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6154 
{\plain \fs24 \f3  \par
}\pard \fs24\tx-1440\tx-720\tx0\tx324\tx1044\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6154
{\plain \fs24 \f3 This is the night, when all who believe in Christ are delivered\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 from the gloom of sin, and are restored to grace and holiness\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 of life.\par
}\pard \fs24\sl120\slmult1\tx-1440\tx-720\tx0\tx324\tx1044\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6154 
{\plain \fs24 \f3  \par
}\pard \fs24\tx-1440\tx-720\tx0\tx324\tx1044\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6154
{\plain \fs24 \f3 This is the night, when Christ broke the bonds of death and hell, \softline
and rose victorious from the grave.\par
}\pard \fs24\sl120\slmult1\tx-1440\tx-720\tx0\tx324\tx1044\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6154 
{\plain \fs24 \f3  \par
}\pard \fs24\tx-1440\tx-720\tx0\tx324\tx1044\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6154
{\plain \fs24 \f3 How wonderful and beyond our knowing, O God, is your\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 mercy and loving-kindness to us, that to redeem a slave, you\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 gave a Son.\par
}\pard \fs24\sl120\slmult1\tx-1440\tx-720\tx0\tx324\tx1044\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6154 
{\plain \fs24 \f3  \par
}\pard \fs24\tx-1440\tx-720\tx0\tx324\tx1044\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6154
{\plain \fs24 \f3 How holy is this night, when wickedness is put to flight, and\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 sin is washed away. It restores innocence to the fallen, and joy\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 to those who mourn. It casts out pride and hatred, and brings\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 peace and concord.\par
}\pard \fs24\sl120\slmult1\tx-1440\tx-720\tx0\tx324\tx1044\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6154 
{\plain \fs24 \f3  \par
}\pard \fs24\tx-1440\tx-720\tx0\tx324\tx1044\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6154
{\plain \fs24 \f3 How blessed is this night, when earth and heaven are joined\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 and man is reconciled to God.\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3  \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 Holy Father, accept our evening sacrifice, the offering of this\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 candle in your honor.  May it shine continually to drive away\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 all darkness. May Christ, the Morning Star who knows no\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 setting, find it ever burning--he who gives his light to all\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 creation, and who lives and reigns for ever and ever.  }{\plain \fs24 \i\f3 Amen.\par
}{\plain \fs24 \i\f3  \par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f3\fs20 It is customary that the Paschal Candle burn at all services from\par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f3\fs20 Easter Day through the Day of Pentecost.}{\plain \fs24 \f3 \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 \par
}\column 
\pard \fs24\tx-1440\tx-720\tx0\tx324\tx1044\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6154
{\plain \fs36 \f3\fs36 The Liturgy of the Word}{\plain \fs24 \f3 \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3  \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 \par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f3\fs20 The Celebrant may introduce the Scripture readings in these or similar\par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f3\fs20 words}{\plain \fs24 \f3 \par
}\pard \fs24\sl120\slmult1\tx-1440\tx-720\tx0\tx324\tx1044\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6154 
{\plain \fs24 \f3  \par
}\pard \fs24\tx-1440\tx-720\tx0\tx324\tx1044\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6154
{\plain \fs24 \f3 Let us hear the record of God's saving deeds in history, how\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 he saved his people in ages past; and let us pray that our God\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 will bring each of us to the fullness of redemption.\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3  \par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f3\fs20 At least two of the following Lessons are read, of which one is always the Lesson from \softline
Exodus.  After each Lesson, the Psalm or Canticle listed, or some other suitable psalm, \softline
canticle, or hymn may be sung.  A period of silence may be kept; and the Collect provided, or \softline
some other suitable Collect, may be said.}{\plain \fs24 \f3 \par
}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20  \par
}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20  \par
}{\plain \fs20 \b\f3\fs20 The story of Creation}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20  \par
}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 Genesis 1:1-2:4a\par
}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20  \par
}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 Psalm 136:1-9,23-26}{\plain \fs24 \f3 \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3  \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 Let us pray.     }{\plain \fs20 \i\f3\fs20 (Silence)}{\plain \fs24 \f3 \par
